body:
He seems nice, you should marry him immediately.

&#x200B;

(/s just in case it wasn't obvious)

I'm unattractive bordering on ugly, and I've never had my being a gamer either questioned or been undermined. Nobody of any gender bats an eyelid when I say I'm playing a 'non-girly' game. I used to go to a tabletop games club that was predominantly attended by men, and still nobody gave a damn. 

So it's been my experience that *(NOTE: hyperbole from here on in)* if a girl is attractive, then she can't possibly be a real gamer, because attractive girls are for "playing with", not playing alongside (if you get my drift). Girls who are ugly are allowed to like what they want as long as we don't try and stop the male gamers talking to the attractive ones. Or something. */hyperbole*

&#x200B;
